{"deleteScheduledEmailReminder/deleteScheduledSMSReminder are async but calls aren't awaited/collected, so reminder cancellations/DB updates can be lost if the handler returns before the promises settle": 0.9669160842895508, "Because cancellations are processed after the earlier delete-by-date logic, if this cron runs late a cancelled reminder could be removed from DB without ever sending the corresponding SendGrid cancellation request": 0.587687075138092, "The SendGrid call assumes reminder.referenceId is always a valid batch id; if it's null/empty (or for non-email rows), this will throw and the reminder won't be deleted, causing repeated failures on subsequent runs": 0.9290411472320557}